abstract: >
  A critical digital edition of the Andong Kwŏn ssi Sŏnghwabo (安東權氏成化譜), the
  oldest extant comprehensive Korean genealogy, printed in 1476: node and edge tables
  of the men it records and the descent and marriage relations among them, the
  facsimile of the Academy of Korean Studies copy (AKS JE A 55020), and a reading
  environment that presents each leaf beside the men it records. The tables are the
  revision of 7 July 2025.
